Z||000000||Gold87SE||11-28-2000||02:09 AM||||Pardon my ignorance but could somebody please tell me what an Indy Fiero is?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||11-28-2000||02:15 AM||||An Indy Fiero is the 1984 Indy 500 pace car Version.  Yes, in 1984 the Fiero was the Pace car for the indianapolis 500 and Pontiac made somewhere around 1500 commerative "Indy Fiero's" to sell to the public.  I own one.  They have a red and light grey interior.  They are awesome!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-28-2000||02:16 AM||||An Indy Fiero Is an 1984 Fiero with the notchback body/ aero nose. (Simular to 85 GT and 86/87 SE. They made 2000 of them in 1984 because Pontiac built 5 REAL pace cars and one was used for the Indianapolis 500 that year. They are white with custom leather seats in gray and red. Although it is only a 4cyl, it is a popular car to get. The real pace cars had a 232hp Super Duty 4cyl and could run up o 144mph. They also had a scoop that went over the roof line. See pic below.<BR>This is one of my Favorite Fiero's. Hopefully one day I will own one. <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_9.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||11-28-2000||02:20 AM||||The Indy was made in 1984.......<BR> <A HREF="http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/indycar2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/indycar2.html</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||10
Z||000004||PearlBlueSoul||11-28-2000||05:57 AM||||Man, you guys suck!  I want that scoop!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>That's a nice one.  wouldn't mind having one of those.  Matter of fact I'm working on building one at the moment.  But, I wouldn't mind having this car either.  TRD's Rally prepped, 700HP 4WD MR2.  <P> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mr2.com/ARTICLE/PICTURES/700hpMkI/700hp.gif"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mr2.com/ARTICLE/PICTURES/700hpMkI/MRprotoXfront.gif"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mr2.com/ARTICLE/PICTURES/700hpMkI/MRprotoXrear.gif"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mr2.com/ARTICLE/PICTURES/700hpMkI/MRprotoXcockpit.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR><A HREF="http://"http://www.atlantamr2s.com"" TARGET=_blank>www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://"http://www.geocities.com/darionscard"" TARGET=_blank>Pics of my car, "Heaven and Hell"</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">  <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Philphine||11-28-2000||10:24 AM||||i was with my brother looking at cars and looked at a similar mr2 on one lot. i dont see why you couldn't use the scoop. might have to trim the bottom to get the right angle and/or measure the height from the engine lid to the roof and do the same on a fiero (just did on an '84. right at 12"), to see how close they are.<P>i read once that up to that year even thought a 4cyl. hadn't paced the indy for a lot of years, it was the fastest pace car up to that time. that would include the '78 corvette pace car.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
